{
  "source": "course-assets/one-more-thing/one-more-thing.mp4",
  "duration": 204.2453125,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.76,
      "text": "Why can the exact same prompt produce a totally different answer?"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.4,
      "end": 7.62,
      "text": "What makes an AI's response more predictable or more varied?"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.36,
      "end": 11.4,
      "text": "And just how much raw math does a single answer require?"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.28,
      "end": 15.42,
      "text": "Let's say you ask an AI, what should I name my new doc?"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.96,
      "end": 18.02,
      "text": "When the AI reaches the actual name,"
    },
    {
      "start": 18.34,
      "end": 22.8,
      "text": "it calculates a probability for every possible word or token in its vocabulary."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.8,
      "end": 26.96,
      "text": "Here, the name spot takes the top position at 22%."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.68,
      "end": 29.54,
      "text": "Because spot is the mathematical favorite,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.04,
      "end": 32.9,
      "text": "you might expect the AI to simply pick it every single time."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.52,
      "end": 36.46,
      "text": "But having the highest probability does not guarantee selection."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.36,
      "end": 42.38,
      "text": "A 22% probability means AI would pick spot about 22 times out of 100 tries,"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.72,
      "end": 44.7,
      "text": "on average, if the odds stay the same."
    },
    {
      "start": 45.36,
      "end": 49.48,
      "text": "Keep those exact probabilities completely unchanged across five separate picks."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.08,
      "end": 51.74,
      "text": "And we might get a varied set like this."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.5,
      "end": 54.6,
      "text": "Pick one is max, pick two is spot,"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.6,
      "end": 58.08,
      "text": "three is buddy, four is Rex, and five is Max again."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.82,
      "end": 60.96,
      "text": "These five picks are just one possible set."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.56,
      "end": 64.1,
      "text": "Spot was picked only once, even with the highest probability."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.98,
      "end": 66.52,
      "text": "Another five picks could turn out differently."
    },
    {
      "start": 67.28,
      "end": 68.72,
      "text": "The best chance is not a guarantee."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.54,
      "end": 73.18,
      "text": "Choosing the most likely token every time makes answers robotic and repetitive."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.2,
      "end": 77.66,
      "text": "Giving other highly ranked tokens a chance to surface adds necessary variety."
    },
    {
      "start": 78.46,
      "end": 81.04,
      "text": "Each token the AI chooses shapes what comes next."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.54,
      "end": 84.24,
      "text": "So what changes how predictable those choices are?"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.9,
      "end": 86.82,
      "text": "The answer is a mechanism called temperature."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.5,
      "end": 91.08,
      "text": "Temperature reshapes the probabilities before AI picks each token."
    },
    {
      "start": 91.7,
      "end": 95.38,
      "text": "In chat GPT, Claude, and Gemini, it's handled for you behind the scenes."
    },
    {
      "start": 96.2,
      "end": 98.48,
      "text": "We begin with the exact same baseline odds as before,"
    },
    {
      "start": 98.88,
      "end": 100.58,
      "text": "with spot at a 22% chance."
    },
    {
      "start": 101.08,
      "end": 104.26,
      "text": "Applying a low temperature mathematically concentrates those odds"
    },
    {
      "start": 104.26,
      "end": 105.52,
      "text": "onto the most likely choices."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.36,
      "end": 109.86,
      "text": "Spot's chance jumps from 22% up to 36%."
    },
    {
      "start": 110.42,
      "end": 112.7,
      "text": "High temperature applies the exact opposite effect."
    },
    {
      "start": 113.32,
      "end": 117.44,
      "text": "It spreads the odds outward, giving less likely choices a much better chance."
    },
    {
      "start": 118.26,
      "end": 120.26,
      "text": "Now Spot's probability drops down to 16%."
    },
    {
      "start": 121.12,
      "end": 124.78,
      "text": "Looking across that top row shows us the core function of the setting."
    },
    {
      "start": 125.68,
      "end": 128.5,
      "text": "Temperature simply changes how far ahead the top choice is,"
    },
    {
      "start": 128.88,
      "end": 130.08,
      "text": "compared to the rest of the pack."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.16,
      "end": 132.16,
      "text": "Temperature reshapes the probabilities."
    },
    {
      "start": 132.86,
      "end": 134.44,
      "text": "It does not change what the model learned."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.36,
      "end": 136.78,
      "text": "Every choice starts with calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 137.9,
      "end": 141.8,
      "text": "AI's training creates its weights, the static numbers that shape every prediction."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.58,
      "end": 145.98,
      "text": "For each new token, AI uses these weights in a massive set of calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 146.76,
      "end": 150.92,
      "text": "Imagine a model using one trillion weights, at roughly two calculations per weight."
    },
    {
      "start": 151.46,
      "end": 154.2,
      "text": "On the left, producing one token, such as Spot,"
    },
    {
      "start": 154.66,
      "end": 157.94,
      "text": "requires one pass through our example model's trillion weights."
    },
    {
      "start": 158.52,
      "end": 160.24,
      "text": "That yields our two trillion calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.26,
      "end": 165.82,
      "text": "Moving to the middle panel, a short answer is about 100 tokens written by the AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 166.54,
      "end": 171.76,
      "text": "100 tokens at 2 trillion calculations each is about 200 trillion calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 172.36,
      "end": 176.4,
      "text": "On the right, a longer conversation takes about 1,000 tokens."
    },
    {
      "start": 176.92,
      "end": 182.8,
      "text": "1,000 tokens at 2 trillion each pushes the math into the realm of two quadrillion calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 183.86,
      "end": 185.98,
      "text": "These counts cover the tokens the AI writes."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.5,
      "end": 189.78,
      "text": "They are estimates for an imagined model, not measurements of a real one."
    },
    {
      "start": 190.3,
      "end": 194.54,
      "text": "But the reality is clear, even a short answer takes trillions of calculations."
    },
    {
      "start": 195.36,
      "end": 199.82,
      "text": "Math and probability, one token at a time, every time you hit send."
    }
  ],
